From: liujixings <liujixings@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: decode L2 encapsulation for native L2B offload

Bridged frames are punted with PPE_CPU_REASON_HIT_UNBIND once the PPE has
allocated a native AN7581 L2B entry, but only HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED was
handled, so bridged PPPoE passthrough, 802.1Q and PHY-to-VLAN flows were
never bound and stayed on the CPU path.

Bind them and rebuild the egress header from a full decode of the frame:
Ethernet, up to two VLAN tags and an optional PPPoE session. Resolve the
bridge master through the ingress VLAN upper for PON/direct GDM parents,
keep transparent bridges untagged internally, derive the egress tag stack
from the forward path (including a VLAN upper egress), and program the
innermost EtherType and IB1 PSN bit. Also stop using ip_hdr() on RX skbs
which have no network header yet.

Signed-off-by: liujixings <liujixings@outlook.com>
---
--- a/include/linux/soc/airoha/airoha_offload.h
+++ b/include/linux/soc/airoha/airoha_offload.h
@@ -11,6 +11,14 @@
 #include <linux/workqueue.h>
 
 enum {
+	PPE_CPU_REASON_NO_FLOW_IS_ASSIGNED = 0x07,
+	PPE_CPU_REASON_UN_HIT = 0x0d,
+	/* The PPE allocated an L2B entry but has not bound it yet. Bridged
+	 * traffic, including non-IP frames such as PPPoE passthrough and
+	 * 802.1Q frames, is punted with this reason and must be bound by the
+	 * CPU before it can be forwarded by hardware.
+	 */
+	PPE_CPU_REASON_HIT_UNBIND = 0x0e,
 	PPE_CPU_REASON_HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED = 0x0f,
 	/* The PPE punts the first packet of a multicast flow so that the CPU
 	 * can fill and bind the L2B entry: the hardware itself never binds
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
@@ -542,6 +542,10 @@
 		u16 sid;
 		u8 num;
 	} pppoe;
+	/* Innermost EtherType carried by a bridged frame, in network byte
+	 * order. Native L2B entries use it to rebuild the egress header.
+	 */
+	__be16 l2_etype;
 };
 
 enum airoha_flow_entry_type {
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
